  "nl_text": "The rschema_0500 database is designed to manage tasks and user roles within an organization. The database consists of six tables: Role_Table, Task_Type, Task_Status, Task_Priority, User, and Task_Table. The Role_Table stores information about different roles within the organization, with each role having a unique ID, a name, and a description. The Task_Type table contains details about the types of tasks that can be assigned, including a unique ID, name, and description. Similarly, the Task_Status and Task_Priority tables store information about the possible statuses and priorities of tasks, respectively. The User table stores information about the individuals within the organization, including their email, password, username, and role ID, with the role ID referencing the Role_Table to establish the relationship between users and their roles. The Task_Table stores information about each task, including its name, description, deadline, assigned user, priority, status, and type, with foreign keys referencing the User, Task_Priority, Task_Status, and Task_Type tables to establish relationships between tasks and these entities. The Task_Table also includes a primary key to uniquely identify each task, and the Assigned_User_ID, Task_Priority_ID, Task_Status_ID, and Task_Type_ID columns are not nullable, indicating that these fields must be populated for each task.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis is a task management system with the following main features:\n1.Task Management:Create, assign, track, and complete tasks.Each task includes:Task ID, Task Name, Task Description, Task Deadline, and Task Progress.Task Type, Task Status, and Task Priority.Each task is assigned to a user.\n2.User Management:Add, delete, and manage users.Each user has a unique User ID, Username, Password, and Email.Each user has a fixed role.\n3.Role Management:Define and assign user roles.Each role includes:Role ID, Role Name, and Role Description.\n4.Task Type Management:Define and manage different task types.Each task type includes:Task Type ID, Task Type Name, and Task Type Description.\n5.Task Status Management:Track task statuses (e.g., To Do, In Progress, Completed), including the status name and description.\n6.Task Priority Management:Set task priorities.Each priority includes:\nTask Priority ID, Task Priority Name, and Task Priority Description.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0500.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0500\nCREATE TABLE `role_table` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_type` (\n  `task_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_type_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_status` (\n  `task_status_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_status_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_priority` (\n  `task_priority_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_priority_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role_table` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `task_table` (\n  `task_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deadline` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `assigned_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_priority_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_status_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `task_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`task_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `task_table_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`assigned_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `task_table_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`task_priority_id`) REFERENCES `task_priority` (`task_priority_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `task_table_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`task_status_id`) REFERENCES `task_status` (`task_status_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `task_table_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`task_type_id`) REFERENCES `task_type` (`task_type_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
